# ExItS Premium UX + Apple HIG

Applies only to ExItS Premium Web (`src/ExItS.Premium/ExItS.Premium.Web`, port 5180). PinoyBusinessPOS rules and files stay unchanged. Do not restyle shipped Premium screens to match this rule.

## Priority

1. Premium design system owns visual identity: `src/styles/tokens.scss`, `[data-theme]`, `[data-palette]`, `[data-radius]`, `[data-density]`, and components under `src/components/`.
2. Apple HIG ([Human Interface Guidelines](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/), [Layout](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/layout), [Dark Mode](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/dark-mode)) guides usability, accessibility, and interaction quality.
3. Do not change business logic or validation to satisfy layout. Do not import PinoyBusinessPOS Org EHG, Personal Soft Glass, or Tailwind into Premium.

## Keep Premium identity

- Reuse Premium Button, Input, Select, Dialog, Toast, Card, Date/Time, and Bottom Sheet. No new UI library.
- Primary follows the active palette. Light, Dark, and System stay on `[data-theme]`.
- Icons stay Material Symbols Rounded. Corners, five elevations, and compact / standard / large density stay on existing tokens.
- Keep current springs and dialog transitions. Do not add Liquid Glass.

## Usability and accessibility

- One primary action per view. Secondary actions are quieter. Destructive actions use the danger treatment and a confirmation.
- Icon-only controls keep their visual size. Give them about a **44×44 CSS px** hit target via padding, not by changing `--control-height`.
- Text and icons meet contrast on the surface they sit on. Focus uses `--color-focus` (primary). Keyboard reaches every action. Icon-only controls have an accessible name.
- Show field errors next to the field. Do not clear input on a failed submit.

## Buttons and interactions

- Use Premium `Button`. One filled primary action; secondary and ghost stay visually behind it.
- Press, hover, and disabled states use existing semantic tokens (`--color-primary-hover`, `--color-disabled-fill`, `--color-disabled-text`).
- Feedback is visible and short. Do not invent a second press animation.

## Layout, safe areas, and keyboard

- Align and group with existing spacing and surface tokens. Reveal secondary detail through the current dialog, sheet, or disclosure.
- Size from the container. The same action must work on mobile, tablet, and desktop. Wrap or scroll on the block axis. Do not clip labels or add a horizontal page scrollbar.
- Keep content inside the safe area. When the keyboard opens, scroll the field into view and leave the primary action reachable.
- Use logical properties (`margin-inline`, `padding-inline`, `inline-start`) so RTL alignment flips. Do not add a language switcher. English remains the catalog.

## Dark Mode

Use `[data-theme="dark"]` tokens. Do not add a second dark palette or hardcoded slate.

- Page, then card (`--color-surface`), then elevated overlay (`--color-surface-elevated`) stay in that order.
- Dialogs, Bottom Sheets, Toasts, menus, and inputs use those surfaces. Inputs stay distinguishable from the sheet behind them.
- Primary stays the palette color for actions and focus, not for large fills.
- Avoid washed-out gray-on-gray, heavy blur, and neon accents.

## Motion

- Motion explains a change, then settles. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Premium `useReducedMotion` follows that setting.
- Do not remove the existing dialog spring or sheet slide for reduced motion; the reduced variants already skip them.

## Do not

- Redesign Premium components or copy PinoyBusinessPOS chrome.
- Add dependencies or `!important` theme overrides.
- Weaken tests to match a visual preference.
